  "notes": [
    "EMBED — Restaurant.menuCategories (with nested items): The primary customer browsing path (REQ-8, REQ-9, REQ-10, REQ-12) reads restaurant + full menu in one document fetch with no joins. Menus are owned exclusively by the restaurant and are managed atomically by the restaurant manager (REQ-34, REQ-35). The bounded nature of a realistic menu (tens of categories, hundreds of items) keeps document size safe. This is the single most latency-sensitive read path and justifies the embed.",
    "EMBED — Order.items: Items are an immutable price snapshot taken at checkout time. Prices must be frozen for dispute resolution, refund calculation, and audit. They are never independently queried. Embedding eliminates any risk of retrospective price drift.",
    "EMBED — Order.statusHistory: The lifecycle has exactly 9 possible states (enum), so history array length is strictly bounded. Embedding supports complete audit trails on a single document fetch without a separate collection.",
    "EMBED — User.savedAddresses: A user owns only a handful of addresses (REQ-6); they are always read with the user; they are never referenced independently. Embedding is safe and efficient.",
    "EMBED — User.agentProfile: Delivery-agent-specific fields (availability, vehicle, live location) are always read together with the user identity for auth and assignment. Embedding avoids a join on the hot assignment path (REQ-25).",
    "REFERENCE — Payment (separate collection): Payment processing is asynchronous (gateway webhooks), PCI-sensitive, and has its own independent lifecycle. Separating it prevents gateway latency from causing write contention on Order documents and isolates PCI audit surface (REQ-21, REQ-22, REQ-23, constraint 1).",
    "REFERENCE — Delivery (separate collection): The real-time tracking service updates agent GPS coordinates on every location ping (REQ-28). A separate focused document prevents high-frequency writes from touching the Order document. It also cleanly models reassignment attempts (REQ-26) and proof-of-delivery (REQ-29).",
    "REFERENCE — Review (separate collection): Admin moderation queries (REQ-33), running-average recomputation (REQ-32), and the one-review-per-order uniqueness constraint (BR-6) are all cleaner against a dedicated collection with a unique index on orderRef.",
    "REFERENCE — Dispute (separate collection): Disputes are independently managed by admins (REQ-41) and may outlive the order's active lifecycle. A separate collection supports admin search and assignment workflows without polluting the Order document.",
    "2dsphere index on Restaurant.location: Required for delivery-radius filtering (BR-4, REQ-8) using MongoDB $nearSphere/$geoWithin. Restaurant.deliveryRadiusKm stores the configurable radius per restaurant (BR-4, constraint 4).",
    "2dsphere index on User.agentProfile.currentLocation: Required for proximity-based agent assignment (REQ-25) using $nearSphere.",
    "Order.commissionRate is snapshotted at order creation time from the effective platform or restaurant-level commission so that settlement (BR-5) is always computable from the order document alone, even if the rate changes later.",
    "PlatformConfig holds the configurable lock duration (REQ-4), session TTL (REQ-3), default delivery radius (REQ-42), commission rate (REQ-42, BR-5), service fee (REQ-42), and agent offer timeout (REQ-26). A single 'key' field allows multiple config version documents if versioning is ever needed.",
    "User.failedLoginAttempts + lockedUntil enforce the account-lockout rule (REQ-4). The max attempt count is driven by PlatformConfig.maxFailedLoginAttempts so it is configurable.",
    "User.isVerified + verificationToken enforce the REQ-2 pre-order verification gate. verificationToken is sparse-indexed for the verification endpoint lookup.",
    "Cart has a TTL index on expiresAt so abandoned carts are automatically purged. The unique compound index on [customerRef, restaurantRef] enforces the one-active-cart-per-customer-per-restaurant rule (REQ-13).",
    "Review.status enum with 'removedByAdmin' value, plus removedByRef/removedAt/removalReason, enforces REQ-33 and BR-7 audit trail for admin review removal.",
    "Order.hasReview boolean provides an O(1) guard against duplicate reviews (BR-6) without an additional query to the reviews collection on every order fetch.",
    "Restaurant.isCodAllowed enforces the REQ-20 business rule that COD is only available where the restaurant permits it.",
    "Delivery.assignmentAttempts array records each offer/decline/timeout cycle (REQ-26) and is bounded by the finite number of available agents, acceptable in practice.",
    "AdminAuditLog covers the RBAC audit trail requirement (tech stack 7.5) logging every privileged action by actor, timestamp, and affected entity.",
    "Money fields use Decimal128 throughout to avoid floating-point rounding errors in financial calculations (subtotals, fees, refunds, commissions).",
    "The schema deliberately omits notification delivery receipts as a separate collection — the requirements reference notifications as an outbound side-effect (REQ-30) handled by the third-party messaging provider; storing receipts is not required by the SRS."
  ],
  "datastore_product": "MongoDB"
}